        "falseColor": false,
        "notes": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with approximate thermal size: 93.93 km effective diameter (catalog ±0.94 km; additional shape and thermal-model uncertainty). Thermal size supplies a volume-scale approximation. No surface imagery exists; rotational phase is illustrative. Gaia DR2 plus Lowell inversion; publication table gives 502 Lowell and 17 Gaia points. One pole is released. This is a coarse convex reconstruction, not a resolved surface. The thermal scale is approximate. Convex inversion supplies broad outline without resolved craters, concavities, reflectance or regolith texture. One mean color for the whole disc (Gaia DR3 reflectance spectrum), scaled to the 5.7% geometric albedo JPL lists; no terrain, albedo pattern or color variation is drawn."
